-- Markup — recursive AST for templates. Ten cases: Text (leaf String),
-- Bold / Italic / Link / Heading (each wrapping a child Markup), Image
-- (src + alt leaf), Paragraph / Fragment / List (each wrapping children
-- as List Markup), and Expr (carrying an Expression for dynamic value
-- interpolation). The Renderable typeclass renders Markup → per-channel
-- output (HTML / plaintext / Telegram MD / PDF) via instance dispatch.
--
-- Static rows: none. Markup is a function-internal type — values flow
-- through `render(markup)` etc. as `{$tag, …}` shapes but no JSONB
-- column stores a Markup row. Pure code refactor.
--
-- Phase 4c of the ts-elimination workstream — see
-- workstreams/ts-elimination/briefs/phase-4c-templates-pilot.md. First
-- per-module flip exercising self-reference at the entity tier: Bold /
-- Italic / Link / Heading carry `child: Markup` and Paragraph / List /
-- Fragment carry `children: List Markup`. The `$named "Markup"` refs
-- resolve lazily through the catalog at validate / display time — same
-- load-order interleaving validated in 4b's Result(AIError, AIResponse)
-- return-type ref.
--
-- `HeadingLevel` is extracted as a top-level refined-Number atom for
-- the same reason as license.fenel's Rate (Phase 4a) and
-- profile_tag.fenel's Importance (Phase 3c): `|`-refinement is a type-
-- decl-level form only and doesn't parse at field-position type-expr
-- slot. Named-atom extraction is the canonical path-(b) workaround.
-- HeadingLevel = enum-over-Number combines Rate's interval form and
-- profile-status atoms' enum-over-String form on a Number base.
--
-- `Expression` named-ref in the Expr case resolves through the engine's
-- core type catalog at validate time; same lazy-$named mechanism as
-- the self-refs.

HeadingLevel = Number | value ∈ {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}

Markup = Text content: String | Bold child: Markup | Italic child: Markup | Link url: String child: Markup | Image src: String alt: String | Heading level: HeadingLevel child: Markup | Paragraph children: List Markup | List ordered: Boolean items: List Markup | Fragment children: List Markup | Expr expression: Expression
